      "element_id": "prisma_2020_11_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_14",
      "quote": "The MMAT [17] appraises the quality by study design type, such as quantitative, qualitative, or mixed empirical methods. We distinguished mixed-methods as studies combining both qualitative and quantitative methods, whereas studies classified as multi-methods used 2 + qualitative methods. The criteria are specific to each type of study, with five domains apportioned to qualitative studies and quantitative studies subdivided into randomized controlled, non-randomized and descriptive studies.",
      "reason": "The domains/components assessed by the tool are described (study-design-specific criteria, five domains for qualitative, subdivisions for quantitative designs)."
    },
